								<div class="title" id="post-title-4850671">
																	<a href="/forum/t-13947857/getting-sandbox-feedback-without-greenlight#post-4850671">Re: Getting Sandbox Feedback without Greenlight?</a>
									</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/zyn" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1404533); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1404533&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608623223" alt="Zyn" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1404533)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/zyn" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1404533); return false;" >Zyn</a></span> <span class="odate time_1608617254 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">22 Dec 2020 06:07</span>
																	<br/>
						in discussion <a href="/forum/c-891087/help:questions-desk">Writing Help / Help: Questions Desk</a> &raquo;
						<a href="/forum/t-13947857/getting-sandbox-feedback-without-greenlight">Getting Sandbox Feedback without Greenlight?</a>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4850671">
									

<p>Agreeing with <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/hexick" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5065702); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5065702&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608617254" alt="Hexick" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5065702)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/hexick" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5065702); return false;">Hexick</a></span>'s post above, and noting that if you're looking to work on your writing skills specific to SCP articles, you don't necessarily need to ask for feedback on a whole draft. If you're seeking to improve clinical tone, for example, you can post short excerpts in the Questions Desk forum to ask for opinions on what to improve. You can also ask for tips on writing certain parts of an SCP article, such as interviews. Examples of such threads include:</p>
<ul>
<li><a href="http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/forum/t-13834538/dialogue-and-interviews">http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/forum/t-13834538/dialogue-and-interviews</a></li>
<li><a href="http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/forum/t-13787438/references-for-ideas-on-interactions-between-foundation-and">http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/forum/t-13787438/references-for-ideas-on-interactions-between-foundation-and</a></li>
<li><a href="http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/forum/t-13696555/containment-procedure-required">http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/forum/t-13696555/containment-procedure-required</a></li>
<li><a href="http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/forum/t-13695935/how-much-is-too-much-detail">http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/forum/t-13695935/how-much-is-too-much-detail</a></li>
</ul>
<p>Oftentimes a draft isn't interesting to a reviewer because the core concept is boring/unwieldy. If you're going to ask someone to review an entire sandbox draft, ideally you'd have an interesting concept written up and not just a throwaway practice premise that might introduce issues that will distract a reviewer from focusing on the writing separate from the concept.</p>

							</div>

								
					
