<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> A giant formless fleshy monstrosity living in the a part of the Bering Sea. While immobile, the creature is sentient, and appears to be in a constant state of distress. When a living human victim is fed to the creature, it will expel the remains of its last victim, and its new victim will take over its body until a new one is fed to it.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> After discovering the creature and its property, the Foundation appoints General Ferguson in charge of containment, who quickly begins cracking down on the anomaly. Soon after, it is found that the SCP can communicate in simple sentences via a special radio frequency, and the foundation discovers that the anomaly is &quot;hungry&quot; and &quot;hurting&quot;, and wants more victims so it can be freed. After this, Ferguson cracks down even more, building a massive concrete wall around the anomaly and ordering constant security, with no one to be anywhere near the creature or have any communication. While many researchers do attempt communication otherwise, they are unable to do much else to help it due to Ferguson's strict orders. Eventually, a d class ends up being fed to it, and there is a massive call among the other d class at the station to feed it another victim to save their comrade.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention Grabber:</strong> After this, Ferguson becomes even more strict, with anyone who sympathizes with the anomaly ordered to be imprisoned for treason against the Foundation. Eventually, years later, the anomaly finally moves from its position and makes a charge for Ferguson in a devastating containment breach, with Ferguson being consumed by the end. After this, nearby Foundation ships pick up distress signals from a scared and pained Ferguson calling for backup. The ships attempt to help, but after being met by heavy d class resistance at the station, they compromise with them and agree that the foundation is allowed back in the site as long as they don't help Ferguson, deciding that his tyrannical actions got him what he deserved.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> Hope this isn't too similar to anything else!</p>

